    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0550" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3430</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Irkutsk</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thomson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d560-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Irkutsk</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 14, 1.22
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Volkov staff received a letter dated December 10 from
                    Japanese General [?] stating that the troops of the Kolchak government may not come eastward any farther than
                    station Slavyanka on Lake Baikal to fight against Semenov. To-day Semenov
                    proclaimed himself commander of the Far Eastern Army. Staff of
                        Volkov claims that telegram from Kato, Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs, to
                        Semenov intercepted two weeks ago
                    states Japanese disapproved Volkov appointment and
                        Semenov must oppose
                        Volkov nomination.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Thomson</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d560-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d560-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Legation in China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
